**Read:** [The fluid mechanics of aerosols — Goodarz Ahmadi, Clarkson](../sources/Fluid-Mechanics-of-Aerosols-Ahmadi.lingua#r_175C6Q2GTKPZJJ6XSRHF5979G0), complete coagulation notes; [Aerosols and coagulation — Chiang C. Mei, MIT](../sources/Aerosols-and-Coagulation-Mei.lingua#r_433KSJ2E60YP29TNWRQV1Z7PS9), derivation and appendices; the primary references for any added kernel or growth process.

Start from explicit pair events and derive a continuous population equation with a declared kernel convention. Track at least total number and material mass. Explain how the measured size convention relates to the modeled classes and how products beyond a finite class range are handled.

**Work:** Compare an exact finite event account, the constant-kernel total-number law and a size-resolved approximation. Test symmetry, nonnegativity, moment conservation, limiting cases and class-range refinement. Introduce either breakup, incomplete sticking or removal and derive the changed balances before calculating.

Use the source disagreement over the factor of two as a scholarly exercise: identify each symbol's definition, count an event once and state the corrected conclusion. Distinguish an algebraic correction from evidence that the simplified kernel models a particular real aerosol.

